From: hmaarrfk <mark.harfouche@conda-forge.org>
Date: 2026-07-25
Subject: third_party: only pull test-only vendored deps when tests are on

Upstream unconditionally `include()`s third_party/cmake/googletest.cmake
and third_party/cmake/yaml-cpp.cmake even though neither dependency is
used by the driver itself:

* googletest is only linked from umd/*/unit_tests/ (gated by
  ENABLE_NPU_UNIT_TESTS, see the companion patch) and from
  validation/test-app-lib/.
* yaml-cpp is only linked from validation/umd-test/.

Both helper modules do try find_package() first, but they fall back to
`add_subdirectory()` on the vendored third_party/googletest and
third_party/yaml-cpp submodules when no system package is found. That
fallback forces downstream packagers to either vendor those sources
(against conda-forge policy) or install test-only dependencies into a
driver-only build just to keep the configure step quiet.

Gate the two `include()`s on the options that actually need them. The
library output of this driver (libze_intel_npu.so) is unchanged.

Paths in this patch are prefixed with `linux-npu-driver/`
because the recipe extracts this source into an explicit
`target_directory`, so patches are applied from one level above the
upstream root.
---
 linux-npu-driver/third_party/CMakeLists.txt | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
diff --git a/linux-npu-driver/third_party/CMakeLists.txt b/linux-npu-driver/third_party/CMakeLists.txt
index da922e0..52f9d59 100644
--- a/linux-npu-driver/third_party/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/linux-npu-driver/third_party/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -14,6 +14,19 @@ if (ENABLE_NPU_PERFETTO_BUILD)
   include(cmake/perfetto.cmake)
 endif()
 
-include(cmake/googletest.cmake)
-include(cmake/yaml-cpp.cmake)
+# googletest and yaml-cpp are test-only dependencies: googletest is
+# consumed by umd/*/unit_tests/ (ENABLE_NPU_UNIT_TESTS) and by
+# validation/test-app-lib/, yaml-cpp only by validation/umd-test/.
+# Both helper modules fall back to add_subdirectory() on the vendored
+# third_party/googletest and third_party/yaml-cpp submodules when no
+# system package is found, so including them unconditionally makes a
+# driver-only build depend on sources it never compiles. Only pull them
+# in when something in the build actually links against them.
+if (ENABLE_NPU_UNIT_TESTS OR ENABLE_VALIDATION_BUILD)
+  include(cmake/googletest.cmake)
+endif()
+
+if (ENABLE_VALIDATION_BUILD)
+  include(cmake/yaml-cpp.cmake)
+endif()
 
